Z||000000||Wannabe||07-10-2000||11:33 PM||||Is anybody using the RCC bump steer kit on a GT? Any feedback or impressions on how effective the kit is?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wannabe||07-11-2000||03:31 PM||||Not too encouraging  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-11-2000||05:58 PM||||I don't suppose many people have installed the kit because I believe you only feel the real benefit if you push the car as in Autocrossing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||07-11-2000||06:19 PM||||Here is a good read about the bumpsteer: <A HREF="http://fierorock.homestead.com/Bumpsteer.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorock.homestead.com/Bumpsteer.html</A> <P>Also is the Black Cat Racing your company?<BR>I need some one offs done for some standard autometter gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||07-11-2000||06:57 PM||||I have the RCC bump steer correction kit on my V8 Fiero. I've been out in the field for work the last couple of days, that's why I haven't answered until now. To be honest, I don't know how well it works by itself. The suspension was all worn out, so I rebuilt the whole thing at once. I love the handling now, but it's probably a combination of new ball joints and tie rods, poly bushings, bump kit, rear coil-overs (also RCC) and front lowering springs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||07-11-2000||10:58 PM||||Thanks for the input guys. I do lots of lapping and time trials, so I think that the kit will be worth the price if it give some extra confidence when diving into high speed corners  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Spyder, I should be able to do those. Send me a note and we can chat.||||reg||1
